// A HANDLER CONFIG DEFAULT IS JUDGED BEFORE WHAT IT CALLS IS DECLARED. The
// default `seed()` is a list, so `k + 1` must refuse with E_TypeMismatch.
// The program checks clean and runs, exiting 17 (measured 2026-09-25): the
// callee-first order never learns that the handler's config default calls
// `seed`, so the default is judged against an unjudged `seed`. Declaring
// `seed` above the handler refuses as it should.
//
// Retires when the default's reference is an edge the declaration order
// reads (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge).
effect Ask {
  ask() -> Int
}

handler answer(k = seed()) {
  ask() => resume(k + 1),
}

fn seed() = [1, 2, 3]

fn body() with Ask = ask()

fn main() = body() ~> answer
